-- Ingest: lift a stream of raw resources (the nested-HAMT payloads yielded by the
-- crawl/manifest/kustomize steps) into a typed graph. Each resource becomes a node
-- colored by its kind and identified by its qualified id Kind/namespace/name
-- (ids.gatwd), carrying the whole resource as its payload so the relation passes can
-- read any field of it. graph_insert_node refuses an id that is already a node: two
-- resources with the same kind, namespace and name are one mistake in the data (the
-- same manifest listed twice, two files defining one object), reported as an
-- [ERROR] naming both - never merged into whichever came last.
def k8s_ingest = fold (\g r -> graph_insert_node (hamt_get "kind" r) (k8s_id_of r) r g) graph_empty
